From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:19:42 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] os: open the console devices by the names Windows 7 accepts

Go 1.23 made os.Stat work on the console devices (CL 560755,
commit 28b8851), and since Go 1.25 os.Stat stops at once when a name is
reported missing (CL 671458, commit bb0c14b). Windows 7 reports CON, CONIN$
and CONOUT$ as missing, and opens them only by their bare names, not as
\\.\CONIN$.

Let os.Stat and os.Open reach the console on Windows 7. When a \\.\ name is
reported missing, try the bare name.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7              Stat or Open of        works
	                       \\.\CONIN$ fails
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 8 and later    works                  works

Gate: query (prefixed name reported missing) | Remembered: N

diff --git a/src/os/file_windows.go b/src/os/file_windows.go
index a7d82e69..9f22413b 100644
--- a/src/os/file_windows.go
+++ b/src/os/file_windows.go
@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@ func openFileNolog(name string, flag int, perm FileMode) (*File, error) {
 	}
 	path := fixLongPath(name)
 	r, err := syscall.Open(path, flag|syscall.O_CLOEXEC, syscallMode(perm))
+	if bare, ok := consoleDeviceName(name); ok && errors.Is(err, ErrNotExist) {
+		r, err = syscall.Open(bare, flag|syscall.O_CLOEXEC, syscallMode(perm))
+	}
 	if err != nil {
 		return nil, &PathError{Op: "open", Path: name, Err: err}
 	}
